st frame of the official MarioGPT interactive demo, showing a Mario-style platform level","https://github.com/shyamsn97/mario-gpt","credit","MarioGPT authors · official demo still","Source reviewed","2026-10-18","verified","section","metadata","Year","2023","year","list","Tracks","ordered",false,[89],"dimensions","2D","Development stages",[93,94,95],"stages","Planning","Engines & scenes","Testing","Topics",[99,100,101,102],"tags","PCG","Level generation","Text-to-level","GPT-2","Further reading",[105],{"_53":106,"_25":107},"Paper","https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.05981","Project source",[110],{"_53":108,"_25":72},"Why it belongs here","Descriptions of enemies, pipes, and elevation become character-grid levels and previews, with an interactive simulator or A* checks available. It generates level content within existing rules and supports research on controllable procedural content generation. Its scope does not include game engines, character art, or complete gameplay code.","detail","guidance","Resource type","Category","2D development","category","lead","summary","name","2d","paper",[132],[99,100,101,102],[129,130,131],[122],2023,"plan","scene","test",{"_53":106,"_25":107},{"_134":135},"documents",{"_136":137,"_138":139},"en",[141,145,146,147,144,148,149,150,151,152,153,154,155,156,157,158,159,160,161,162,163,164,165,166,167,168,169,170,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,143,180,142,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,197,198,199,200,201],"zh",[140,141,142,143,144],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies","native-operation-details","production-debugging-contracts","production-coverage-gaps","generative-tools